Step 1 — Create the GitHub files
Open your Generative-AI-Laboratory repository.

Select Add file → Create new file, and create each of the five files inside:

Experiment-07-Text-Image-Conversion/
Step 2 — Set up Python
Open the experiment folder locally in VS Code.

Create a virtual environment:

python -m venv .venv



Activate it on Windows PowerShell:

.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1



Step 3 — Install dependencies

python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt



Step 4 — Run the experiment
Option A — Run both tasks

python text_image.py --mode both



Option B — Generate an image only

python text_image.py --mode text-to-image --prompt "A robot reading a book in a library"



Option C — Generate a caption from an existing image

python text_image.py --mode image-to-text --image sample.jpg




For a quick lab demonstration on a computer without a GPU, Option C is the more practical starting point because BLIP captioning is substantially less demanding than Stable Diffusion image generation.
Step 5 — Verify the results
Open the outputs/ folder and check the generated files.

For text-to-image, inspect generated_image.png. For image-to-text, open generated_caption.txt and compare the caption with the actual image.
